      "id": 1,
      "text": "Reliance grew around the Hiwassee River, where a water‑powered grist mill and sawmill first sparked the community in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reliance%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Louisville and Nashville Railroad arrived in the late 1880s, turning Reliance into a bustling stop for workers, tourists, and entrepreneurs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://theforgottensouth.com/hiwassee-lodge-church-reliance-tennessee/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Hiwassee Union Church and Masonic Hall, built in 1899, once served as a church, lodge, and school all in one frame building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://theforgottensouth.com/hiwassee-lodge-church-reliance-tennessee/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A ferry that began in the 1870s was replaced by a one‑lane truss bridge in 1912, which later became part of State Route 315 after a 1992 replacement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reliance%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Reliance’s Hiwassee River offers whitewater adventures that rival famous rivers like the Ocoee, yet it stays free of the usual crowds.",
